Windows 11 computer to automatically empty the Recycle Bin using a feature
called Storage Sense.

Enable and Configure Storage Sense

1. Open Settings: Press the Windows Key + I to open the Settings app. 
2. Go to Storage: In the Settings menu, click on System and then
select Storage. 
 
3. Enable Storage Sense: You will see a toggle switch for Storage Sense. If it&#39;s
off, click it to turn it on. 
 
4. Configure Cleanup Schedule: Click on Storage Sense to open its
configuration page. 
 
5. Set Recycle Bin Cleanup: Look for the option that says, &quot;Delete files in my
recycle bin if they have been there for over&quot; and select your preferred time
frame from the drop-down menu. You can choose from 1, 14, 30, or 60
days. 
 
Once you have completed these steps, Windows will automatically delete files
from your Recycle Bin based on the schedule you have set.
